                    <h1 id="doc-section">🚀 IIS Deployment Management (SiteDeploy)</h1>
                    <blockquote>
                        <strong>One-line summary</strong>: An efficient operations tool for IIS automated deployment, centralized multi-server release, one-click backup, and fast version restore.
                    </blockquote>

                    <h2 id="en-features">✨ Features</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>🌍 Multi-language support</strong>: Built-in Simplified Chinese and English switching for global teams.</li>
                        <li><strong>📦 Core publishing workflow</strong>: One-click package, upload, overwrite, and IIS restart.</li>
                        <li><strong>🌐 Multi-node coordination</strong>: Unified management for single-host and multi-server cluster deployment.</li>
                        <li><strong>🛡️ Safety and rollback</strong>: Automated backups and rapid restore for near-instant rollback on failure.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><img src="./images/pub_1.gif" alt="Publishing Demo"></p>

                    <h2 id="en-install">🛠️ Installation & Configuration</h2>

                    <h3 id="en-single">🖥️ 1. Single Server Deployment (IIS Mode)</h3>
                    <ol>
                        <li><strong>Download and extract</strong>: Download the main-node package <code>SiteDeploy.zip</code>, then extract it to <code>C:\inetpub\wwwroot\SiteDeploy</code>.</li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Configure application pool</strong>:
                            <ul>
                                <li>Name: <code>sitedeploy</code></li>
                                <li>.NET CLR version: <code>No Managed Code</code></li>
                                <li>Managed pipeline mode: <code>Integrated</code></li>
                                <li>Advanced settings: change <strong>Identity</strong> from <code>ApplicationPoolIdentity</code> to <strong><code>LocalSystem</code></strong>.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Add website</strong>:
                            <ul>
                                <li>Site name: <code>SiteDeploy</code></li>
                                <li>Application pool: select <code>sitedeploy</code></li>
                                <li>Physical path: <code>C:\inetpub\wwwroot\SiteDeploy</code></li>
                                <li>Port: custom (for example <code>8080</code>)</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Access and initialize</strong>:
                            <ul>
                                <li>URL: <code>http://localhost:8080</code></li>
                                <li>
                                    <strong>Login credentials</strong>:
                                    <ul>
                                        <li>Username: <code>admin</code></li>
                                        <li>Initial password: check <code>admin_initial_password.txt</code> in the site root directory.</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Configuration reference (<code>appsettings.json</code>)</strong>:
                            <ul>
                                <li><code>SystemConfig.Urls</code>: configure child-node URL addresses.</li>
                                <li><code>SystemConfig.IpWhitelist</code>: IP allowlist for access restriction.</li>
                                <li><code>BindUrl</code>: current site binding URL (required for Windows Service mode, optional in IIS mode).</li>
                                <li><code>BasePath</code>: base path of the site.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                    </ol>

                    <h3 id="en-multi">🌐 2. Multi-Server Deployment (IIS Mode)</h3>
                    <blockquote><strong>Prerequisite</strong>: Ensure the main node has been deployed and is running correctly.</blockquote>
                    <ol>
                        <li><strong>Download and extract</strong>: Download the child-node package <code>SiteDeploy.Node.zip</code>, then extract it to <code>C:\inetpub\wwwroot\SiteDeploy.Node</code>.</li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Configure application pool</strong>:
                            <ul>
                                <li>Name: <code>sitedeploy.node</code></li>
                                <li>.NET CLR version: <code>No Managed Code</code></li>
                                <li>Managed pipeline mode: <code>Integrated</code></li>
                                <li>Advanced settings: change <strong>Identity</strong> from <code>ApplicationPoolIdentity</code> to <strong><code>LocalSystem</code></strong>.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Add website</strong>:
                            <ul>
                                <li>Site name: <code>SiteDeploy.Node</code></li>
                                <li>Application pool: select <code>sitedeploy.node</code></li>
                                <li>Physical path: <code>C:\inetpub\wwwroot\SiteDeploy.Node</code></li>
                                <li>Port: custom (for example <code>8081</code>)</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Verify child node</strong>:
                            <p>Visit <code>http://localhost:8081</code>. If the page displays the current site URL properly, configuration is successful (child nodes do not provide a login page).</p>
                            <p><strong>Configuration reference (<code>appsettings.json</code>)</strong>:</p>
                            <ul>
                                <li><code>SystemConfig.IpWhitelist</code>: IP allowlist restriction.</li>
                                <li><code>BindUrl</code>: binding URL for Windows Service mode (optional in IIS mode).</li>
                                <li><code>BasePath</code>: site base path.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Link to main node</strong>:
                            <p>In main-node <code>appsettings.json</code>, add child-node URLs to <code>SystemConfig.Urls</code> (for example: <code>http://localhost:8081</code>).</p>
                        </li>
                    </ol>

                    <h3 id="en-proxy">🔄 3. Reverse Proxy Configuration (High-Security Environments)</h3>
                    <blockquote><strong>Best for</strong>: If your environment does not allow changing the app pool identity to <code>LocalSystem</code>, use reverse proxy mode instead.</blockquote>
                    <ol>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Update configuration (<code>appsettings.json</code>)</strong>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Set reverse proxy bind URL <code>BindUrl</code> (for example: <code>http://127.0.0.1:5002</code>).</li>
                                <li>Set site base path <code>BasePath</code> (for example: <code>sitedeploy</code>).</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Install and start Windows Service</strong>
                            <p>Run the <code>install-service.bat</code> script in the root directory as Administrator.</p>
                            <p>Make sure this URL is accessible in browser: <code>http://127.0.0.1:5002/sitedeploy</code>.</p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Configure IIS reverse proxy</strong>
                            <p>Ensure IIS has reverse proxy modules installed (<strong>URL Rewrite</strong> + <strong>Application Request Routing (ARR)</strong>).</p>
                            <p>Create an empty folder: <code>C:\inetpub\wwwroot\SiteDeploy-Proxy</code>.</p>
                            <p>Create a new IIS site, bind a port (e.g. <code>8080</code>), and set physical path to the folder above.</p>
                            <p>Replace the site <code>web.config</code> with:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?&gt;
&lt;configuration&gt;
  &lt;system.webServer&gt;
    &lt;security&gt;
      &lt;requestFiltering&gt;
        &lt;requestLimits maxAllowedContentLength="209715200" /&gt;
      &lt;/requestFiltering&gt;
    &lt;/security&gt;
    &lt;rewrite&gt;
      &lt;rules&gt;
        &lt;rule name="ReverseProxyInboundRule1" stopProcessing="true"&gt;
          &lt;match url="(.*)" /&gt;
          &lt;action type="Rewrite" url="http://127.0.0.1:5002/sitedeploy/{R:1}" /&gt;
        &lt;/rule&gt;
      &lt;/rules&gt;
    &lt;/rewrite&gt;
  &lt;/system.webServer&gt;
&lt;/configuration&gt;</code></pre>
                        </li>
                        <li><strong>Access the system</strong>: Open <code>http://localhost:8080</code> in browser.</li>
                    </ol>

                    <h2 id="en-usage">💡 User Guide</h2>
                    <h3 id="en-login">🔑 System Login</h3>
                    <blockquote>⚠️ <strong>Note</strong>: Always log in from the main node. Child nodes do not provide login UI.</blockquote>
